****
Dark plages, dark spots, bright flares, and prominences, perhaps even filaments when dense enough. 

The ionized iron Sun was one of the surprises I came across. 
With basically no amateur coverage (few to none venture far from the few well known lines, and none make atlases),
I didn't know what aspect to expect. 
Professional literature indicated prominences and flares, and I found those indeed. 
But I didn't expected the plages to be so dark, against a disk so overall weird.

One of the wavelengths that propelled me to cover a great portion of the spectrum, and put together this Atlas.
